<%# Crossing the supports limit changes what every other card in the phase should show - a
    support button or the limit notice - but only the clicked card is re-rendered by the vote
    response. The buttons carry the ids of the cards that were on screen, so refresh exactly
    those; the controller leaves @proposals blank when the phase has no limit.

    Mirrors budgets/ballot/lines/_refresh_ballots, which does the same for ballot lines.

    show_share_popup comes back from the card that was clicked, so a sibling the user had already
    supported keeps its share popup instead of losing it to the refresh. %>
<% (@proposals || []).each do |proposal| %>
$("#<%= dom_id(proposal) %>_votes").html('<%= j render Proposals::NewVotesComponent.new(proposal, show_share_popup: @show_share_popup, proposal_ids: @proposal_ids) %>');
<% end %>
